{"id": "tea:brahmavidya-upanisad:2-9", "source": "src:brahmavidya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2-9"}, "paraphrase": "Oṃ's body: a is the Ṛgveda, the gārhapatya fire, the earth and Brahmā; u the Yajurveda, the dakṣiṇa fire, the mid-space and Viṣṇu; m the Sāmaveda, the āhavanīya fire, the sky and Īśvara.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "concepts": ["cpt:omkara-matras"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text brahmavidya-upanisad 2-9"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 2-9 located in the e-text; the passage matches the paraphrase.", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:brahmavidya-upanisad:27-31", "source": "src:brahmavidya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "27-31"}, "paraphrase": "The disciple should do whatever the guru says without deliberating; then, having gained knowledge, he may abandon caste, stage of life and even the Vedas like dust; the guru is Hari himself.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:guru"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text brahmavidya-upanisad 27-31"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 27-31 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'tasya dāsyaṃ sadā kuryātprajñayā parayā saha | śubhaṃ vā'śubhamanyadvā yaduktaṅguruṇā bhuvi || 27 ||…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:brahmavidya-upanisad:51-53", "source": "src:brahmavidya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "51-53"}, "paraphrase": "Three kinds of teacher: the codaka who points out the path, the bodhaka who shows the place, and the mokṣada who gives the supreme; addressed to Gautama.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-acaryas"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text brahmavidya-upanisad 51-53"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 51-53 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'brahmahatyāśvamedhādyaiḥ puṇya-pāpairna lipyate | codako bodhakaścaiva mokṣadaśca paraḥ smṛtaḥ || 51 ||…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
